 "notes": [
  "Measured: traced the supplied developer plan after enlarging plan and table crops. No photographs were supplied.",
  "Derived: scale 57 pixels per metre, supported by living width 328 pixels / 5.750 m, bedroom width 290 pixels / 5.100 m, and living depth 191 pixels / 3.350 m; bathroom 145 pixels / 2.550 m also agrees.",
  "Printed: table gives hall 2.3, living room 16.8, bedroom 14.2, bathroom 4.6 and balcony 3.4 square metres; total 41.3 square metres. Printed dimension strings are transcribed separately, not computed from polygons.",
  "Measured: the hall and living/kitchen have no dividing wall. The hall/living polygon boundary is assumed solely to label their continuous floor. Kitchen is part of living room.",
  "Measured: balcony connects to living and bedroom through two drawn door swings. Exterior entrance is the door on the recessed west edge of the hall. Bathroom and bedroom doors occupy the full drawn gaps.",
  "Measured: room polygons retain structural column recesses and the bathroom and entrance steps. Wardrobes and kitchen furniture are not treated as full-height partitions.",
  "Assumed: 2.60 m ceiling, 2.10 m doors, 0.80 m window sills and 1.50 m window heights, because no photographs or elevation dimensions were provided. All floor and wall colours are neutral placeholders, not observed finishes.",
  "Assumed: the thin balcony exterior edge is a 1.10 m parapet/guard; represented as a 2.60 m wall with a full-width opening above the guard to satisfy the wall-height range. Its construction and height cannot be determined from the plan.",
  "Derived: dimensions describe maximum spans; irregular room outlines and columns mean area is not simply the product of the printed spans. Preserve printed areas even where tracing differs.",
  "Derived correction: hall/living open floor division adjusted to give the printed hall area of 2.3 square metres. Door threshold floor strips meet at the wall centreline. Flagged exterior wall stretches trimmed or stepped to follow the room edges."
